/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:2087:      "docstring": "Complete a visible crop into the shared 20x20 binary motif in its matching orientation.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid is a two-color rectangular crop of one rotation/reflection of the same 20x20 motif.\n- One color is the motif foreground and the other color is the motif background.\n\nRule:\n- Try each input color as the foreground mask.\n- Match that mask against every possible window in every dihedral orientation of the motif.\n- Repaint the uniquely matched full 20x20 motif with the matched foreground/background colors.\n\nKey insight:\n- The examples are partial windows of one canonical binary pattern; the local crop is distinctive enough to identify the full orientation and offset.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:2092:        "dst": "the full 20x20 motif in the matching rotation/reflection and window position",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:2179:        "window",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:2180:        "windows",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:8706:      "docstring": "Recolor a path-network by adjacent seed regions.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Path color P forms a thin orthogonal network with a solid square hub (NxN).\n- Seed colors appear in colored regions (non-bg, non-P) adjacent to path branches.\n\nRule:\n- Infer P as the non-bg color whose largest component is most network-like.\n- Find the largest solid k×k all-P square (the hub); exclude it from recoloring.\n- Recolor each path branch to the seed-region color it touches most.\n- Recolor the hub center pixel to the seed whose branches touch the hub most.\n\nKey insight: The hub stays uncolored; branches inherit color from adjacent seed regions by adjacency count.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:8710:        "src": "path-network pixels s (thin largest component) + seed regions s (non-bg, non-path)",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:8711:        "transform": "recolor each path branch (connected component of s excluding the hub square) to the majority color of the seed region it touches; keep the hub square, but recolor its center to the seed color that touches the hub most"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:8786:        "seed",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:9758:      "docstring": "Fill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\n- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\n\nRule:\n- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\n- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\n- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\n\nKey insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:9871:        "seed",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:9872:        "seeded",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:22022:      "docstring": "Fill every row from the nearest marked horizontal bar, turning bar rows and color-boundary ties into separator rows.\n\nInput structure\n- A dominant background fills the grid except for full-width horizontal bars and one vertical marker column.\n- Outside the marker column, every row is monochrome: either background or a source bar color.\n- Background rows share one marker color in the marker column; source bar rows share the other.\n\nRule\n- Each non-source row takes the color of the nearest source bar, with that row's marker-column pixel set to the source-marker color.\n- If a row is exactly midway between nearest bars of different colors, make the whole row the source-marker color.\n- Each original source bar row becomes a source-marker row with the marker-column pixel changed to the background-row marker color.\n\nKey insight\n- The marked bars are horizontal seeds for a one-dimensional nearest-seed partition over rows; equal-distance rows are separators only when the competing seed colors differ.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:22110:        "seed",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:22111:        "seeds",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26460:      "docstring": "Expand the top-left seed mask into a recursive colored pattern and tile it across the full grid.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- All foreground lies in a top-left rectangle whose last row and last column are a solid secondary color.\n- Removing that secondary-color row and column leaves a seed region containing background plus one primary color.\n\nRule\n- Use the primary-color pixels in the seed as a binary mask.\n- Replace each primary seed cell with a copy of the seed mask in the primary color, and each background seed cell\n  with a copy of the seed mask in the secondary color.\n- Repeat and crop that expanded tile to the original grid shape.\n\nKey insight\nThe solid L-shaped secondary-color border is a legend, not output content; it supplies the color used when the\nseed's background cells are expanded.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26464:        "src": "top-left seed region containing background and one primary color, with a solid secondary-color L-shaped legend border",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26465:        "transform": "expand the seed mask once: primary seed cells become primary-color copies of the mask, background seed cells become secondary-color copies, and mask background stays background; tile/crop the expanded pattern to the full grid"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26545:        "seed",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28834:      "docstring": "Rebuild the foreground rectangles as a largest-to-smallest lower-left nesting.\n\nInput structure\n- A periodic wallpaper background is overlaid by foreground colors that each form a rectangular frame or solid rectangle.\n- The largest foreground rectangle is the output frame; smaller foreground rectangles are the objects to nest inside it.\n- A frame may be partially hidden by a smaller rectangle, but its visible pixels still determine its bbox.\n\nRule\n- Ignore the wallpaper and crop the result to the largest foreground rectangle's bbox size.\n- Sort foreground rectangles by bbox area from largest to smallest.\n- Reconstruct each frame or solid rectangle, placing every next smaller rectangle in the lower-left of the current rectangle's usable region.\n\nKey insight\n- The scattered background colors are not objects; the meaningful order is the unique descending rectangle size chain, and each step nests into the previous rectangle's lower-left interior.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28838:        "src": "foreground rectangular frames and solid rectangles over periodic wallpaper",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28840:        "transform": "discard the wallpaper; sort rectangles by bbox area descending; rebuild each frame or solid rectangle, placing each next smaller rectangle at the lower-left of the current frame interior or solid bbox",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28951:        "wallpaper"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29937:      "docstring": "Extend the diagonal blue ray through the grid, reflecting it off red line-segment mirrors.\n\nInput structure\n- Black-background grid with one diagonal 8-connected blue ray seed.\n- Red foreground objects, when present, are straight horizontal or vertical mirror segments.\n- Other foreground bars are transparent to the ray and may be overwritten where the ray crosses them.\n\nRule\n- Start from the ray seed endpoint whose outward diagonal extension remains inside the grid.\n- Paint the ray continuously in that diagonal direction until it leaves the grid.\n- If the next cell is a red mirror, do not paint it; reflect by flipping the row direction on a horizontal mirror or the column direction on a vertical mirror.\n\nKey insight\n- The non-red bars are decoys: only red bars reflect the diagonal path, while all other crossed cells become blue.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29941:        "src": "diagonal blue ray seed",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29942:        "path": "continue from the only in-bounds seed endpoint; red horizontal or vertical bars reflect the diagonal ray; stop when the reflected ray leaves the grid",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30040:        "seed",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31879:      "docstring": "Complete the framed area by expanding the unique upper template that contains the existing seed pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- A teal background contains small colored template masks above a larger rectangular frame.\n- The frame encloses one fill color arranged as a partial block-scaled copy of one template.\n- The frame interior dimensions are an integer square scale of the matching template bbox.\n\nRule:\n- Crop to the rectangular frame.\n- Identify the unique upper template whose block-scaled mask covers every existing fill pixel inside the frame.\n- Reset the frame interior to background and paint the whole scaled mask with the fill color.\n\nKey insight:\nThe lower colored pixels are seed cells that reveal which upper template should be completed inside the frame.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31884:        "dst": "rectangular frame interior d containing partial fill-color seed pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31885:        "match_cond": "block-scaled s contains all seed pixels in d",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31886:        "transform": "clear dst to bg and paint the full matched scaled mask with the seed color",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31976:        "seed",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:37442:      "docstring": "Grow an alternating pink/orange triangular trace downward from the horizontal orange seed row.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a green background and one horizontal row containing all orange foreground pixels.\n- The seed row may contain isolated orange pixels and adjacent orange runs.\n- Pink is absent from the input and is used for the first generated row.\n\nRule:\n- Copy the input grid.\n- Two rows below the current active row, place a child pixel between each active pair\n  whose middle cell in the current row is background.\n- Alternate generated row colors between pink and orange, stopping when no children\n  can be generated or the next row would leave the grid.\n\nKey insight:\n- Only an active-background-active triplet in the current row reproduces; contiguous\n  active runs do not produce children through occupied middle cells.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:37446:        "src": "horizontal orange seed row on green background",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:37534:        "seed",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:45064:      "docstring": "Complete every colored sprite by applying the union of all aligned partial sprite masks.\n\nInput structure:\n- The dominant color is the background.\n- Each non-background color appears as a separated partial copy of one common sprite mask.\n- The copies share a top-left-aligned sprite window; some copies may be missing lower or right edge pixels.\n\nRule:\n- Crop each same-color mask to its bounding box.\n- Pad the crops to the maximum observed height and width, aligned at the top-left, and OR them into one complete template.\n- Fill that template at every sprite location using the sprite's own color.\n\nKey insight:\n- No single input sprite is complete, but their missing cells are complementary, so the aligned union reveals the full mask.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:45068:        "src": "same-color partial sprite masks, one per foreground color, sharing a top-left-aligned window",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:45069:        "transform": "pad smaller masks down/right to the largest observed window, recover the complete sprite as the union of all aligned masks, then fill that mask in each sprite window using that window's color"
